No idea, mainly because I wasn't aware that camxes made such a change, but
you can solve the confusion by spelling them {-ki,ui}, which would be
pronounced as intended under either. People asked a similar question about
my name, but unlike {iui}, {aio} sounds pretty much the same either way, so
my response was simply "it doesn't matter".


On Sun, Sep 7, 2014 at 2:12 PM, Alex Burka <durka42@gmail.com> wrote:

>  Yesterday, I went to the farmers' market and bought some kiwi berries.
> Then, I entered some stage-3 fu'ivla for kiwi fruits and kiwi berries (they
> are different, as I learned yesterday!) into jbovlaste. I spelled them
> {grutrkiui} and {jbarnkiui}. It may be relevant to note that there is
> already a stage-3.5 fu'ivla for kiwi bird, but spelled {cpirkivi}.
>
> Wuzzy raised a good question, which is whether my new fu'ivla {grutrkiui}
> is pronounced ?{grut,r,ki,ui} or ?{grut,r,kiu,i} (and similarly for the
> other one). Of course I intended the former pronunciation. And I think
> that's the correct one, given the current morphology. But it seems to me
> the answer would be different using the old CLL morphology. My reasoning is
> below. Do you agree?
>
> CLL version: it pretty clearly says in section 3.5 that "[w]hen more than
> two vowels occur together in Lojban, the normal pronunciation pairs vowels
> from the left into syllables". So in "iui", the first "iu" would be grouped
> together as a diphthong, leaving "i". There are some problems with this,
> but then again that's why we have a new morphology! Moving on...
>
> camxes version: from here
> <http://www.lojban.org/tiki/Morphology%3A+syllables>. If [kiu] were the
> second-to-last syllable, then bare [i] would be the last syllable, but that
> would be an empty onset. Empty onsets are filled by pauses, but that can
> only happen at the beginning of a word. Therefore, it can only be split
> into syllables as -[ki]-[ui]. QED(?).
> (Full disclosure: this explanation was constructed to fit the facts after
> testing to see how camxes parsed the word.)
>
> mu'o mi'e la durka
